{%- comment -%}
  The file table: files directly in the directory, then its subdirectories.
  Included by subgraph.liquid; reads `files`, `subdirs` and `summary`.

  A subdirectory row says WHAT IT IS when the caller resolved a description
  for it. Otherwise it points at the subdirectory's own README, or says that
  nothing describes it — and never prints a file count (bean `ba9e`). A count
  drifts on every commit that adds a file: one line of `beans/README.md`
  conflicted three times in a single day (2026-10-01), and 207 such counts in
  54 READMEs made almost every merge conflict. The numbers are in the
  writer's `Plan.counts`, for a harness to publish where they cannot conflict.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if summary != "" -%}
_{{ summary }}_

{% endif -%}
{%- if files.size == 0 and subdirs.size == 0 and summary == "" -%}
_This directory holds no files yet._
{%- else -%}
| file | what it is | used by |
|---|---|---|
{% for f in files -%}
| [`{{ f.path }}`]({{ f.href }}) | {{ f.what }} | {{ f.usedBy }} |
{% endfor -%}
{% for d in subdirs -%}
| [`{{ d.name }}/`]({% if d.readme != "" %}{{ d.readme }}{% else %}{{ d.href }}/{% endif %}) | {% if d.description != "" %}{{ d.description }}{% elsif d.readme != "" %}described in its own README{% else %}_nothing declares what this holds_{% endif %} | |
{% endfor -%}
{%- endif %}
